---
description: Commit finished work and push to origin without waiting to be asked.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Push always

When you finish a change in this repo, commit the relevant files and `git push origin HEAD`. Do not wait for “push” or “commit”.

- Never force-push.
- Never skip hooks.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, `.claude/`, or unsolicited docs (`PROJECT_DESCRIPTION.*`, `START_HERE.md`).
- If the working tree is clean, do not create an empty commit.
- If push is rejected because `origin/main` moved (collector commits), pull/rebase then push again. `frontend/data/bundle.json` is regenerated daily and is safe to discard with `git checkout -- frontend/data/bundle.json` if it blocks the pull.
